From 08e6d688169ba084021ee3a00c250b506ac09962 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 22:14:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09775/11362] [outer-loop] Widen five adversarial_verify
 guards; refute two audit findings

The 2026-08-23 QA-layer audit returned six SILENT_NON_FIRING and one REAL_BUG
against adversarial_verify.py. Five are real and are fixed here. Two are not,
and saying so plainly matters more than the fixes: the brief that carried this
work described four of the seven as principle-wrapper blindness recurring, and
that reading does not survive contact with the code.

REFUTED, with evidence. _numeric_pairs does ignore a principle-wrapped number
when called directly -- but no caller calls it directly. verify_artifact
normalizes every top-level {"principle", "value"} wrapper before any check
runs, which is the 2026-07-02 exp5161 fix. Measured: a wrapped tautology pair,
a wrapped pair nested inside `metrics`, and a bare pair all produce the same
TAUTOLOGY flag, and 49 corpus artifacts carry two or more wrapped numeric
top-level fields that depend on this. The origin bug is fixed and stayed
fixed; the reviewer was shown one function with no caller.

_declares_terminal_artifact_readiness was reported blind to a readiness
declaration wrapped at the PAYLOAD level. No artifact has that shape -- the
convention wraps individual fields -- and a wrapped `status` FIELD, which 58
artifacts do carry, still triggers the check. REQ-INFRA-6262 also makes
principle-wrapped values gate-INELIGIBLE deliberately, so unwrapping here
would contradict a spec'd requirement rather than fix a bug.

Both refutations are pinned by tests anyway. A refutation nothing guards is
one refactor from becoming true.

FIXED, each with a regression test named for the audit's own input:
- _is_finite_number accepted only int/float, so numpy.float32(0.913) as an
  in-memory `auroc` silently skipped every numeric check. Now numbers.Real,
  with the bool carve-out intact. It also raised OverflowError on an integer
  too large for float -- a predicate that crashes takes the verifier down on
  one oversized number in one artifact.
- _is_timestamp_field classified `checkpoint_mtime_delta_ns` (real, in
  exp5039) as a wall-clock instant, removing a measured span from tautology
  detection. Interval words now win over the instant markers. `runtime_ms`
  goes with it: "time" inside "runtime" was exempting a duration.
- _is_count_field did not recognize `folds` -- the fold count of a
  cross-validation, exactly what its docstring describes. Ten sibling count
  nouns were missing with it.
- _is_chance_floor_score did not recognize `permuted`, half the project's
  vocabulary for a shuffled-label control, in a list claiming to hold all of
  it.
- check_terminal_artifact_readiness matched "capstone" inside "noncapstone",
  so an artifact whose name says it is not a capstone inherited the capstone
  exemption and lost its critical flag. Same class as "diffusiongemma_met"
  matching inside "meta_tensor".
- The returned report read honest_verdict from the pre-normalization payload,
  reporting an empty verdict for the 155 artifacts that wrap it -- the exact
  field the origin incident was about.

CORPUS MEASUREMENT, all 5775 results/experiment_*.json before and after: 2
artifacts change, ZERO flags added anywhere. exp4716 loses a critical
TAUTOLOGY on held_out_variant_attempts == min_held_out_variant_attempts ==
100, a budget and the value that met it. exp5211 drops two of three duplicate
TAUTOLOGY flags on counts over the same 120-row pool and stays quarantined by
the third. Both removals inspected by hand and both are false positives.

MUTATIONS, each deleted then restored byte-identically: numeric widening
(3 failed / 6 passed), count words (7/9), interval guard (2/3), permut marker
(1/4), capstone boundary (1/2), verdict unwrap (1/2). All six RED mutated,
GREEN restored, sha256 unchanged.

DEFERRED, deliberately. Two of the audit's over-exemption counterexamples are
NOT fixed here: `unshuffled_x` matching the `shuffled` marker, and `count`
matching inside `discounted_return`. Both remove exemptions rather than add
them, both measure zero corpus change today, and an un/non negation guard can
itself over-correct on a name like `unshuffled_control_auroc`. They are a
separate decision with no evidence either way, not a side effect of this one.

The eight test failures in this area are pre-existing: the same eight fail at
HEAD with this file reverted, driven by exp6228 now carrying
flagged_adversarial, not by anything here.

